# Troubleshooting

**Prerequisites:** none beyond [docs prerequisites](/docs/start/prerequisites/).
**Kind:** troubleshooting landing.
**Next:** [Diagnostics](/docs/reference/diagnostics/).

Start with the exact error and the smallest command that reproduces it. Rocci
maps parser diagnostics to source; Roc type errors map back from generated
code where source-map segments exist.

| Symptom | Page |
| --- | --- |
| `roc` missing, Cargo/Roc version skew, Windows unverified | [Install](/docs/troubleshooting/install/) |
| Parse, lower, or Roc type-check failures | [Compile](/docs/troubleshooting/compile/) |
| Handler 404/308/500, Datastar no-op, trailing slash | [Runtime](/docs/troubleshooting/runtime/) |
| Preview window, WebKitGTK, Dev Console empty | [Preview](/docs/troubleshooting/preview/) |

Rocdown catalog codes (`RD2101`, …) and `rocdown check` failures belong on the
[Rocdown](/rocdown/) lane, not here.

If the issue persists, reduce it to one `.rocci` file and include the command,
platform, Roc nightly (`docker/install-roc.sh`), and complete diagnostic in a
repository issue.
